---
import ModelExplorer from './ModelExplorer.astro';
---
<section class="vision-section" id="vision" aria-labelledby="vision-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="vision-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Vision</p>
        <h2 id="vision-title">From local models<br />to data center systems.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="vision-intro">
        <p class="vision-lead">Local hosting is our starting point.</p>
        <p>We're building automatic runtime tuning for models on your own hardware. Our longer-term ambition is to extend that control to model serving across shared compute and, eventually, the data center.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ol class="growth-stages" role="list" aria-label="Our intended expansion path">
      <li>
        <p class="growth-stage-label">Current focus · In development</p>
        <h3>Local model hosting</h3>
        <p class="growth-description">Host models on one machine and automatically adjust memory, batching, and concurrency. Start by making that control loop useful, observable, and reliable.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="growth-stage-label">Expansion path</p>
        <h3>Shared model serving</h3>
        <p class="growth-description">Extend the foundation to teams running multiple models across multiple machines. Coordinate workload placement, request queues, and capacity across shared compute.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="growth-stage-label">Long-term ambition</p>
        <h3>Data center systems</h3>
        <p class="growth-description">Connect model serving and runtime decisions to scheduling, hardware, networking, power, and thermal constraints. Work toward coordinated control of the full system.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="growth-foundation">The strided control loop carries forward: <strong class="strided-emphasis">observe the workload, adjust within limits, and verify the result.</strong> Expanding its scope will require shared scheduling, workload isolation, production reliability, and operator controls.</p>

    <div class="vision-model" id="local-model">
      <div class="model-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Starting with local hosting</p><h3>The workload changes.<br />The settings follow.</h3></div>
        <p>Explore a local host with 24 GiB of GPU memory. Choose a workload to see an example of how context limits, request slots, and memory allocation could adapt.</p>
      </div>
      <ModelExplorer />
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .vision-section { background: var(--paper-card); padding-block: var(--section-space); }
  .vision-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; }
  .vision-heading .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .vision-intro { padding-top: 42px; max-width: 520px; }
  .vision-lead { font: 400 27px/1.45 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .vision-intro > p:not(.vision-lead) { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; margin-top: 21px; }
  .growth-stages { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 56px; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 48px 0 0; }
  .growth-stage-label { font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .growth-stages h3 { font-size: 29px; }
  .growth-description { margin-top: 18px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; }
  .growth-foundation { max-width: 980px; margin-top: 32px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; }
  .vision-model { margin-top: 72px; }
  .model-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .model-heading .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .model-heading h3 { font-size: 29px; }
  .model-heading > p { max-width: 540px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  @media (max-width: 950px) { .vision-heading, .model-heading { gap: 40px; } .growth-stages { gap: 32px; } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .vision-heading, .model-heading { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .vision-intro { padding-top: 0; }
    .vision-lead { font-size: 25px; }
    .growth-stages { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; margin-top: 36px; }
    .growth-stage-label { margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .growth-description { margin-top: 12px; }
    .vision-model { margin-top: 48px; }
    .model-heading { gap: 16px; }
  }
</style>
